# Frame by Frame constraints

`docs/implementation-plan.md` is the source of truth for v1. `docs/design-system.md` locks visual values. `docs/prd.md` locks behavior. When a task departs from them, say so in the journal and in the reply.

- TypeScript strict. No `any`. No non-null assertions on parsed data.
- Do not install `three` or `@designcodeio/threeui`. Atmosphere stays the vendored files in `src/vendor/threeui/`.
- Learning routes (`/plan`, `/week/:n`, `/library`, `/toolkit`, `/capstone`) load zero canvas code. One WebGL surface at a time.
- `scripts/assert-bundle.ts` fails the build if the entry graph exceeds 160KB gzip, or if `three` or `crtRenderer` is in that graph.
- Business logic lives in `src/lib/` as pure functions. Storage is injected. Components render; they do not decide progress rules.
- Icons are Lucide only. No emoji.
- Do not invent a color, type size, space, radius, duration, or font. Use the tokens already in `src/styles/tokens.css`.
- `--accent-warm` is for progress and completion only. Never on a link, button, filter, or nav item.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — warm accent used as a call to action
<button style={{ background: "var(--accent-warm)" }}>Start</button>

// ✅ GOOD — primary actions use the structural accent
<button className="page-button">Start week 1</button>
```
